  "finding": "According to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, for the full year of 2025, a total of 2,289 confirmed measles cases were reported in the United States. CDC reports noted this was the highest number of measles cases since 1992, when 2,126 cases occurred. In 2019, previously the highest post-elimination year, 1,274 individual cases were confirmed. With 2,289 cases, 2025 exceeded both the 1992 tally of 2,126 and the 2019 tally of 1,274.",
